Negative control for the wrapper's `:ajv` seam.

Drops the binding that hands the engine headless's configured Ajv. The
wrapper is the SOLE supplier -- FormProps declares `ajv?: Ajv` and the
wrapper takes Omit<FormProps,"ajv"> -- so without it JSONForms builds its
own default instance and silently loses headless's custom keywords,
phone and domain_name validation among them.

MUST red: validator > "rejects a value only headless's own Ajv knows how
to reject". The paired bare-engine twin MUST stay green; if both red, the
test is reading ambient state rather than the seam.
